  "summary": "The paper reports freestanding Ti3C2Tx films made by LiF/HCl etching of Ti3AlC2, followed by delamination and vacuum-assisted filtration. Four thickness-controlled films (1.0, 4.0, 11.0, and 21.0 \u00b5m) were fabricated; electrochemical thickness-series data are reported for the 4, 11, and 21 \u00b5m devices. The 21 \u00b5m Ti3C2Tx film is the headline electrode, delivering 340 mF cm\u22122 at 0.25 mA cm\u22122 based on two working electrodes. The highest reported volumetric capacitance, 183 F cm\u22123, belongs to the 4 \u00b5m film; mass loading, BET surface area, porosity, pore size, tortuosity, and gravimetric capacitance were not reported."
}